        "id": 1382,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "かた and たほうがいい are distinct grammar patterns both containing 方 (which can be read as かた or ほう) but have different meanings and structures. かた attaches to the verb stem and means 'way of doing (A)' or 'how to (A)', e.g. 書き方 'way of writing' or 'how to write'. In contrast, たほうがいい connects to the past tense of a verb and is used to give advice or make suggestions.",
